# API standards

## Paths

- Base path `/api/v1`. Use plural nouns (`/tickets`, `/tickets/{id}/comments`).
- Status changes: `PATCH /api/v1/tickets/{id}/status` with `{"status": "..."}`.
- Field updates: `PATCH /api/v1/tickets/{id}`.

## Status codes

- `200` OK.
- `201` Created, with a `Location` header.
- `204` No Content.
- `400` validation failure.
- `404` not found.
- `409` invalid state transition.
- `500` unexpected error.

## Errors

- Error bodies follow RFC 7807 Problem Details: `type`, `title`, `status`, `detail`, `instance`.
- Validation failures also include `errors`: an array of `{field, message}`.

## Lists and payloads

- List endpoints accept `page`, `size`, `sort`, keyword search `q`, and status filter `status`.
- Timestamps are ISO-8601 UTC. Enums are `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` strings. JSON fields are camelCase.

## Docs

- Document every endpoint with springdoc-openapi.
